2. Pattern matching

How it was before
Using instanceof always required an explicit cast.
            if (obj instanceof String) {
                String s = (String) obj;
                System.out.println(s.length());
            }        
What changed in Java 17
Java 17 combines type checking and casting into one step.
            if (obj instanceof String s) {
                System.out.println(s.length());
            }        
Why it’s better
  Less boilerplate
  Safer code
  Better readability
